WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.099
(audience applauding)

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:02.043
- Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.043 --> 00:00:04.227
We've got Jane Fonda, Lily Tomlin,

00:00:04.227 --> 00:00:07.246
and Sasheer Zamata with us.
(audience applauds and cheers)

00:00:07.246 --> 00:00:09.450
It's a great day.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.020
- We've been talking a lot
today about female friendships,

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:13.310
what makes a good friend,

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:15.450
and how important women are to each other.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.080
We see that in every episode

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.340
of Jane and Lily's Netflix
show "Grace and Frankie."

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.990
Seriously, you gotta watch it.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:23.240
Meanwhile, on Sasheer's
podcast with Nicole Byer,

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.270
she asked some important questions

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.250
about how far we go for a best friend,

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.350
like, you know, would you murder for me?

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.083
And that would be a hard pass. Nope.

00:00:33.692 --> 00:00:35.350
So, it's time for a quick segment.

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:36.317
We are calling

00:00:36.317 --> 00:00:37.823
"I'd do anything for friendship
but I won't do that."

00:00:39.778 --> 00:00:43.331
♪ I would do anything for friendship ♪

00:00:43.331 --> 00:00:46.417
♪ But I won't do that ♪

00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:47.250
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.010
That's a new one. Nicely done.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.680
Okay. So I'm gonna hit this button.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:53.350
It's so expensive 'cause, yeah.

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.250
It's our super computer, and it will hack

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.520
into the national friendship
database, that totally exists,

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.600
to pull out another
tough test of friendship.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:02.700
Then we're gonna all say,

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.350
if we would do that for
our best friend or not.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.250
Here's where we find
out who we really are.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.400
Here we go.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.233
Okay.

00:01:11.807 --> 00:01:12.772
(bell dings)

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:13.750
Would you...

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:15.505
Oh, hell no!

00:01:15.505 --> 00:01:16.937
(all laughing)

00:01:16.937 --> 00:01:17.780
Would you...

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:19.110
No.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.470
Would you carry a baby for nine months

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:22.890
for your best friend?

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.380
No!
(audience laughing)

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:26.276
I didn't wanna carry mine.

00:01:26.276 --> 00:01:27.109
(all laughing)

00:01:27.109 --> 00:01:27.942
They were...

00:01:27.942 --> 00:01:28.775
It was hell.
- Yeah.

00:01:28.775 --> 00:01:30.690
- I don't know, but pregnancy is not cool.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.460
It's not cool for some of us.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:33.293
Would you do that?

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:34.560
- I love being pregnant,
- Dude.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.920
- but at this point in life,

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.157
I would say to my best friend,

00:01:38.157 --> 00:01:40.240
"Listen, my cells and hormones

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.652
and everything can barely
keep up with myself."

00:01:42.652 --> 00:01:43.950
(Kelly laughs)
"I wouldn't be able to,

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:46.870
maybe if Kelly Clarkson sang
to my stomach everyday."

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:47.790
- [Kelly] Oh, my God.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.130
- I haven't got the wherewithal

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:50.950
to carry my best friend's baby.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:51.947
- I can't. What about you, Lily?

00:01:51.947 --> 00:01:53.820
- But you should have had a baby.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:56.370
- Lily, would you do that?
- No, no. It's all right.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.850
No, I could have...

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:01.104
I've got a doll that like
makes me think it's a baby.

00:02:01.104 --> 00:02:02.374
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:02:02.374 --> 00:02:03.207
- You got one of those?
- Yeah.

00:02:03.207 --> 00:02:04.712
- And that doesn't sound creepy at all.

00:02:04.712 --> 00:02:07.345
(Lily and Kelly laughs)

00:02:07.345 --> 00:02:09.328
(audience applauding)

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:10.610
Good thing.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:11.960
Wait, let's do another one.

00:02:15.261 --> 00:02:16.094
(bell dings)

00:02:16.094 --> 00:02:19.810
Okay. Would you lie to
Congress for your best friend?

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:21.160
Hell no.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.787
- No. I might lie for my worst friend.

00:02:23.787 --> 00:02:26.511
(all laughing)

00:02:26.511 --> 00:02:30.380
(audience applauding)

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.170
- That's awesome. What a great answer.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.130
Jane, what about you? (laughs)

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.680
- Yeah. I like her answer.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.923
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:39.166
- How about you?
- I mean, they lie to us.

00:02:39.166 --> 00:02:41.655
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:02:41.655 --> 00:02:44.019
I feel like I can reciprocate. (chuckles)

00:02:44.019 --> 00:02:45.400
- I feel like I do one.
- [Sasheer] Yeah.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.970
I can lie a little bit.
- I would not.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:49.910
I don't lie, and I do not keep secrets.

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:50.890
Don't tell me.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:51.900
I hate secrets.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.630
They weigh on me like more
weight that I don't need.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:55.600
So here we go.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:56.433
Another one.

00:02:58.745 --> 00:02:59.578
(bell dings)

00:02:59.578 --> 00:03:01.100
If you caught your friend's spouse, ooh,

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.060
if you caught your
friend's spouse cheating,

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.090
would you tell her?

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:06.590
Now, I've done this.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:09.810
I've told my friend, and
it didn't work out for me.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:10.810
- Oh.
- Yeah.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.030
But, didn't end up working
out for her either.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:14.292
But, like...
- Yeah.

00:03:14.292 --> 00:03:15.692
(audience laughing)

00:03:15.692 --> 00:03:16.525
- But it-
- Was it like

00:03:16.525 --> 00:03:18.280
a mind your business kind of thing?

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.350
- It was just like I don't
think I was believed.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:21.630
I don't think they believed me.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.740
And it was one of those-
- Go and message her.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.810
- Yeah.
- Yeah. And I was like,

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:25.643
you know what?

00:03:25.643 --> 00:03:27.740
It's worth it though,
because I would want to know.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:28.580
I would want someone

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.120
to tell me.
- Yeah.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.450
- 'Cause if you ever been that fool...

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:32.620
I've been that fool, too,

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:34.290
- Aw.
- that didn't know.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.180
Have you been that fool?

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.013
- Oh, yeah.

00:03:36.013 --> 00:03:37.350
- Yeah. That sucks.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.620
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:40.393
- So that's why I would
tell. Would you tell?

00:03:40.393 --> 00:03:41.900
- Oh, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:44.470
- I would introduce you to each other.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:46.344
- I would introduce to talk about it.

00:03:46.344 --> 00:03:49.670
(Kelly laughs and applauds)

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:52.152
- No, because...
(audience applauding)

00:03:52.152 --> 00:03:55.260
(Kelly laughs)
(audience applauding)

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.800
- No, if you were both
suffering, I would just...

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.593
That might give you a clue.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:03.460
If I said, "Hey, you know,
you need to meet Kelly,

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:04.680
and Kelly should meet you."

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:05.997
- And then I'll just start talking, yep.

00:04:05.997 --> 00:04:07.620
- [Sasheer] "You have a lot in common."

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.420
- You're sneaky.
- Let them figure it out.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:10.260
(audience laughing)

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:11.630
- Yeah. You're like a sneaky helpful.

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:12.650
- Yeah.
- That was nice.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:14.150
I like that, sneaky helpful.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:15.360
Okay. Okay. What would you do?

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.193
Would you tell?

00:04:16.193 --> 00:04:17.470
- I would 100% tell.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:19.953
I would tell if I just saw him out.

00:04:19.953 --> 00:04:20.817
(Kelly laughs)
Just like,

00:04:20.817 --> 00:04:23.026
"He was at the grocery
store, did you know?"

00:04:23.026 --> 00:04:24.383
(Lily laughs)
- Would you say alone?

00:04:25.426 --> 00:04:26.259
(all laughing)
Driving home.

00:04:26.259 --> 00:04:27.092
- Yeah.
- "He was alone."

00:04:27.092 --> 00:04:29.955
- "He was alone, getting
hotdogs by himself."

00:04:29.955 --> 00:04:31.750
(all laughing)
- [Lily] Good answer.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.280
- Oh, my God. It's a solid answer.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:34.590
Thank you ladies so much.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:35.843
We learned a lot here, people.

00:04:35.843 --> 00:04:36.676
(audience cheering and applauding)

